{
  "id": "80578",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "pH of a Buffer Solution after Adding Acid or Base",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "What occurs on the molecular level in a buffered solution when a strong acid or base is added? Let's look at a buffered solution containing acetic acid (HC"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ") and sodium acetate (NaC"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "). The major species in this solution are: "
              }
            ],
            "id": "lzyocynd17x569e",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "HC"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",   Na"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",   C"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "-"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",   H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wuw8gch9ucvjmmn",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "rlqqjngtn2ps8lf",
            "type": "callout"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When a strong base is added to the solution, the OH"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "-"
              },
              {
                "text": " will react with the weak acid, HC"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", according to the following equation:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "sttljbxbtioryf8",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "wcuizigyuw4hair",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "sefhz16i5ndpmge",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{OH}^-\\;+\\:{\\mathrm{HC}}_2{\\mathrm H}_3{\\mathrm O}_2\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O\\;+\\;{\\mathrm C}_2{\\mathrm H}_3{\\mathrm O}_2^-",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Since OH"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "-"
              },
              {
                "text": " is a strong base this reaction will proceed to completion until all of the OH"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "-"
              },
              {
                "text": " has been consumed. Thereby, decreasing [HC"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] and increasing [C"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "-"
              },
              {
                "text": "]. After these changes are accounted for, the pH of the resulting solution can be calculated as previously discussed. "
              }
            ],
            "id": "hchrk26ne6b7aqz",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The two main steps to these problems:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "722g29o8mch41jy",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "fdxc7nm7epujiy4",
                    "text": "Use stoichiometry to determine the changes resulting from the addition of the strong acid or base"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "u5wpxlh3s9fl363",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "o8ri7rckms9q0aq",
                    "text": "Solve the equilibrium problem with the adjusted initial concentrations. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8cnfw053ul0uast",
                "type": "li"
              }
            ],
            "id": "f1dbo74t77qiffa",
            "type": "ul"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3819217491",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
